stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: The three autonomy modes
  accDescr: The operator starts the master in one of three modes, finish and stop when they name none. Autonomous keeps taking queue rows until the queue is empty or every row waits on a decision. Finish and stop lands what is in flight and takes nothing new. One ticket lands one and reports. Any mode stops on an unexplained red check or a safety rule and reports; the operator's go starts it again.
  state "Autonomous" as Auto
  state "Finish and stop" as Finish
  state "One ticket" as One
  state "Stopped, report sent" as Stopped
  state "Blocked, operator asked" as Blocked
  [*] --> Finish : default
  [*] --> Auto : keep going
  [*] --> One : one ticket
  Auto --> Finish : finish and stop
  Auto --> Blocked : unexplained red or safety rule
  Finish --> Blocked : unexplained red or safety rule
  One --> Blocked : unexplained red or safety rule
  Auto --> Stopped : queue empty or all rows blocked
  Finish --> Stopped : in-flight tickets landed
  One --> Stopped : ticket landed
  Blocked --> Stopped : reported
  Stopped --> Auto : operator's go
